module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_gate_sized_for_the_largest_subject_refuses_every_smaller_one

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_gate_sized_for_the_largest_subject_refuses_every_smaller_one: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_gate_sized_for_the_largest_subject_refuses_every_smaller_one" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an admission gate is sized for the largest subject its producer can take and is applied to every subject regardless of size, so a small subject the host could serve trivially is refused wherever the host cannot serve the largest one. The refusal is correct for the subject it was measured on and an over-prohibition for every other (DESIGN section 4d, second arm: forbidding more of the world than the cited variables support).",
    "HARM: the producer's positive controls cannot execute on the required route, so its capability is either inflated (a constant read as Clear with only refusal arms exercised) or honestly demoted with no required evidence route at all - and the over-prohibition is invisible because the refusal wears the shape of a resource limit rather than a modeling gap.",
    "RECEIPT: v1.stage0 cli_run emit_host compile_xl1_primary_root_tap gates on memory_governor whole_corpus_compile_admission before discovery. At filing the gate was a fixed DECLARED_WHOLE_CORPUS_COMPILE_MEASURED_DEMAND_BYTES against the host budget for ANY source root; gunbc#11265 keyed it on the ROOT's own measured row in gunbc.whole_corpus_compile_demand_projection, which moves the fact from one constant to one row per measured root and leaves the class standing for every root without a row (a fixture root refuses RefusedUnmeasuredRoot, the drop gunbc#11265 declares) - the subject is still not sized. On a session host the tap answers Xl1PrimaryRootObserved over the eleven-module fixture root dag/test/fixture/reference_derived_graph in 25 ms; on the required floor mid-run (gunbc#11461 run 35074340220, then run 35079253040 after the controls moved to a long home) the same two controls refused in under 300 microseconds - the admission, not the emitter - and the floor executes a CHANGED witness once even in a long home, so no enrolment of the Observed arm can be green on that route while the gate stands.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable - a constant sized for the whole corpus refused every smaller root, and the XL-1 producer reported CaptureBlocked with its Observed-arm controls withdrawn. RUNG NOW: mechanically preventable. gunbc#11265 replaced the constant with one row per measured root (gunbc.whole_corpus_compile_admission whole_corpus_compile_measured_root_demands, joined by root identity), so a subject is admitted on its own measurement and never on another root's; the invalid state - one figure applied to every subject - has no constructor left in the admission, and what remains writable is a root with NO row, which refuses as unmeasured rather than being admitted or extrapolated. That is a refusal, not the over-prohibition: the measurement is the remedy the refusal names.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed - an admission keyed by the SUBJECT's measured demand (the closure the tap will compile, sized before the compile), so a fixture root is admitted where the whole corpus is refused, and the whole-corpus figure is one row of that function rather than its only value.",
    "RECEIPT OF THE CLIMB: the XL-4 fixture root with dag/std as its pool was measured by gunbc measure-root-demand and its row authored (whole_corpus_compile_xl1_fixture_root_demand, replayed through gunbc.root_demand_measurement measured_for_root_from_receipt by test.claim.root_demand_measurement_witness); the required floor then executed the tap's Observed arm over it at preparation (gunbc#11461 run 35181521483, prepared-effect-input-acquire xl1_fixture_root_tap disposition=Xl1PrimaryRootObserved) with both controls green in test.claim.legacy_repair_tap_live_bridge_witness, and legacy_baseline_capture_capability reads CaptureAvailable on that receipt. Those controls stay enrolled as the regression evidence (DESIGN 4b(4)).",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, THE RESIDUAL CAPABILITY: structurally guaranteed needs a demand that is DERIVED from the subject rather than looked up by root identity - a measured-demand producer keyed on the closure the compile will take (its module count and source bytes as the row already records), so that a root nobody measured by hand is priced by construction and the unmeasured-root refusal has nothing left to refuse. The instrument that would produce it is the .dag entry point gunbc.whole_corpus_compile_admission whole_corpus_compile_measured_demand_note already names as its own next-rung trigger (scope + target in, exit status + peak out, in one carrier). Owner unassigned at filing (memory_governor and the admission model are the self-host lane's).",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
